  "notes": [
    "pandas is an optional adapter: with pandas absent the analysis still reads these calls off the AST. The confidence is PROBABLE throughout because `frame` is only known to be a dataframe by how it is used."
  ],
  "proves": "Each column is its own lineage node in the feature namespace. `spread` is fed by `ask` and `bid`; `mid` by the same two through `assign`; `rank` by `spread` through `apply`; `symbol` is read as a merge and groupby key without being written. Tracking the *frame* instead of the columns would make every column an input to every other one -- which is the same as having no lineage at all.",
